{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v2","paper":"erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface","excerpts":[["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:denom","Denominator exclusion from a fixed Farey\nwindow","<p><em> If <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>\nthen its reduced denominator exceeds </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mn>79</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>639</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>646</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>646</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>701</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>375</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>323</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>355</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>774</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>875</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>831</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>053</mn><mo>≈</mo><mn>7.96</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Equivalently, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> differs from every rational number\nwhose reduced denominator is at most <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></span>. The bound is sharp for this window:\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> is the exact first\nfailing denominator. It is the denominator of the mediant of two\nexplicit unimodular Farey neighbours.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:deposits","Finite certificate computations","<p><em> <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝒞</mi></mrow></math></span> has been verified\nat: the <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>28</mn></math></span> diagonal instances of\nthe least-common-multiple diagonal through <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></math></span>; all shifts <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></span> simultaneously at <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, by <code>decide</code>; and eight further period\nexamples at <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn></math></span>. These are\nhistorical subsets of the examples. The supplied source also proves a\ncomplete diagonal band for <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>82</mn></math></span>, with no omitted scales. This is bounded coverage, not a\ncofinal diagonal family. Note the quantifier order: the simultaneous\nsmall-shift example uses one pair <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></math></span> for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>16</mn></math></span>. In symbols, it proves <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>N</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>L</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>h</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>16</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo><mrow><mi>𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. In contrast, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>Sep</mi></mrow></math></span> requires arbitrarily large\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi></math></span> for each positive <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi></math></span>; neither the shift range nor the\nbasepoint threshold is bounded.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:sign","Positivity does not exclude an\ninteger","<p><em> Put <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>lcm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. For\nevery <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>8</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>J</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.</mn></math></span></div>\n<p><em> This needs no\nirrationality hypothesis. If this difference is an integer and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> satisfies </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> lies strictly\nbetween <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></msup></math></span>. The later tail difference is a\npositive integer. Its negative, not the carry itself, is the\nrepresentative near zero. Thus positivity locates the residue near the\nupper endpoint; it does not establish the central-residue inequalities.\nBoth restrictions on <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi></math></span> are part of\nthis conclusion.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:rank","Rationality forces unbounded carry\nrank","<p><em> If <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span> is rational then,\nfor every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi></math></span>, the carry sections\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">↦</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>e</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup></math></span> span a rational vector\nspace of dimension at least <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>. The lower bound holds at every\ndepth. It comes from the linear independence of the <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>e</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> retained dyadic totient sections\nfor <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, proved using the Chinese\nremainder theorem and Dirichlet’s theorem, so the full family spans an\ninfinite-dimensional space, the case <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> of Coons’s non-regularity theorem\n(§<a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#sec:mahler-defect\">10.8</a>).</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:period-not-rank","Periodicity modulo an integer does\nnot bound rational rank","<p><em> If <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi></math></span>\nis rational, the same carry <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>u</mi></math></span> has\nunbounded rational section rank and one eventual period modulo <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>v</mi></math></span> valid for all its dyadic sections. More\nprecisely, there are <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></span> such that, for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≡</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mspace width=\"1em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>mod</mi><mspace width=\"0.333em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nThe rank and periodicity assertions hold together. This conditional\ntheorem alone is not a counterexample to a general periodicity-to-rank\nimplication: its antecedent is not established. The rational comparison\nsequence with sum <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span> gives a\ncounterexample to a rank upper bound based on rationality alone; see\nSection <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#sec:mahler-defect\">10.8</a>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:iffs","Equivalent certificate conditions","<p><em> Put <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>lcm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>.\nSeveral variations of Definition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#defn:sep\">1.2</a> are equivalent to <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>. One may allow a\npositive multiple of each prescribed shift, still requiring certificates\nbeyond every basepoint threshold (Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#catalogue:cert:b2\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#catalogue:cert:b2\">6.48</a>). Alternatively,\none may use the original quantified condition or restrict to <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></math></span> at arbitrarily large <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi></math></span> (Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#catalogue:cert:b3\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#catalogue:cert:b3\">6.49</a>). Replacing the\nsymmetric residue test by </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> also gives equivalent\nquantified conditions, including its restriction to <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></math></span> at arbitrarily large <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi></math></span>. Finally, the counted phase-separation\ncondition in Proposition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#prop:b2\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:b2\">2.7</a>(b) is equivalent to\nirrationality. These equivalences change the form of the arithmetic\nquestion, not its logical strength.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:parity","A rational sequence preserving size\nbounds, parity and aperiodicity","<p><em> There is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>6</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span> for all <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span>, <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≡</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.444em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>mod</mi><mspace width=\"0.333em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> for <em>every</em> <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span>, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span> not eventually periodic; indeed for\nevery <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></math></span> there are <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi></math></span> pairs of coefficients <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> starting beyond <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi></math></span>, with starting positions pairwise\nseparated by more than <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>G</mi></math></span>; and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>n</mi></munder><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:radixresidue","Residue series in every integer\nbase","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> be an\ninteger.</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><em>For every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math></span>\nis irrational (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/wcook04/plectis-erdos/blob/24edbddbe2bd68e920327a701aad0b9dd0d69675/lean/ErdosProblems/Erdos249/PaperCompleteR7/RationalIntegerRadixClassification.lean#L128\" data-link-kind=\"exogenous\" rel=\"external noopener\"><code>radix_residue_series_irrational</code></a>).</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>For <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>,\nthe series <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math></span>\nis rational exactly when <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi></math></span> is\nconstant on the even residue classes, and its value is then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow></math></span>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/wcook04/plectis-erdos/blob/24edbddbe2bd68e920327a701aad0b9dd0d69675/lean/ErdosProblems/Erdos249/PaperCompleteR7/RationalIntegerRadixClassification.lean#L145\" data-link-kind=\"exogenous\" rel=\"external noopener\"><code>rational_zmod_radix_observable_iff</code></a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/wcook04/plectis-erdos/blob/24edbddbe2bd68e920327a701aad0b9dd0d69675/lean/ErdosProblems/Erdos249/PaperCompleteR7/IntegerRadixObservables.lean#L303\" data-link-kind=\"exogenous\" rel=\"external noopener\"><code>positiveRadixValue_eq_of_even_constant</code></a>).</em></p></li>\n</ol>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:dilations","Finitely many dilations","<p><em> Let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> be an integer.</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><em>For every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span>, the\nnumbers <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math></span>,\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo></math></span>, are linearly\nindependent over <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span> (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/wcook04/plectis-erdos/blob/24edbddbe2bd68e920327a701aad0b9dd0d69675/lean/ErdosProblems/Erdos249/FiniteDilationLinearIndependent.lean#L42\" data-link-kind=\"exogenous\" rel=\"external noopener\"><code>linearIndependent_one_and_least_residue_values</code></a>).</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi></math></span> be a finite set of\npositive integers, and for <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></math></span>\nlet <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>.\nFor every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>, the\nnumber </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> is\nrational exactly when every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></math></span> is\nconstant on the even residue classes (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/wcook04/plectis-erdos/blob/24edbddbe2bd68e920327a701aad0b9dd0d69675/lean/ErdosProblems/Erdos249/FiniteDilationMixedModuli.lean#L95\" data-link-kind=\"exogenous\" rel=\"external noopener\"><code>rational_mixed_moduli_with_constant_iff</code></a>).</em></p></li>\n</ol>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:slowmoduli","Slowly growing dyadic moduli","<p>Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>κ</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> satisfy\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, and put\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup></math></span>.\nThen <span class=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math></span> is\nrational exactly when <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> for all\nlarge <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span>. In particular the sum is\nirrational when <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> for\ninfinitely many <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi></math></span>.</p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#lem:gsound","A residue certificate excludes an integral\ntail difference","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> satisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span> for all <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span>. For <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mrow><mi>𝒞</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#lem:gperiod","Generic tail-period law","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> satisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span> for all <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span>. If <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></msup><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi></math></span> a positive odd integer, and if <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> satisfies <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>∣</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span>\nfor every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>e</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:gamma","A rational sequence agreeing with any\nfinite totient prefix","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi></math></span> be integers. Define <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>γ</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> by\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>:=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\".2em\" columnalign=\"left left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>P</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>n</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>P</mi><mo>∤</mo><mi>n</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\" symmetric=\"true\"></mo></mrow><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Then:</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><em><span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span> for all\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span>, so <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>γ</mi></math></span> lies in the same coefficient class\nas <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>φ</mi></math></span>;</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em><span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>\nfor every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></math></span>, and consequently\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>φ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>\nfor every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></math></span>;</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em><span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>P</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>, and the odd part\nof its reduced denominator is <em>exactly</em> <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>P</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>;</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em><span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mrow><mi>Sep</mi></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msub></math></span> is\nfalse; indeed it fails already at <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></math></span>.</em></p></li>\n</ol>\n<p><em>Hence for every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi></math></span> there is a\ncoefficient sequence in the same class, agreeing with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>φ</mi></math></span> on all of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></span>, whose quantified condition is\nfalse.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#cor:b1","The limit of a finite-prefix\nargument","<p><em> No proof rule uniform over all <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span> can establish <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>Sep</mi></mrow></math></span> from a single fixed prefix\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>:</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>: Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#thm:gamma\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#thm:gamma\">2.4</a> supplies a rational\ncountermodel with that same prefix. This does <em>not</em> invalidate an\nargument that uses the fixed arithmetic sequence <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>φ</mi></math></span> together with compatible\ninformation at arbitrarily large horizons; the theorem gives a different\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math></span> for each <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi></math></span>, not one sequence agreeing with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>φ</mi></math></span> at every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:b2","Three particular equivalences","<p><em></em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><em><em>Certificate completeness.</em> The complete residue tests\nconsidered here are equivalent to the corresponding nonintegrality\nassertions. Rewriting the quantified condition using one of these\nequivalences does not weaken it.</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em><em>A selectable two-point sample.</em> The condition is as\nfollows. For every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></span>, choose <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>16</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></msup></math></span>, a nonempty set <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>T</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span>, a set\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>T</mi></math></span> of ordered\npairs, and a real number <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. With <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, require\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>T</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> This condition is\nequivalent to irrationality. For the converse, irrationality and the\ndoubling map allow <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> and\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> at\narbitrarily large <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi></math></span>, with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></math></span>. The numerical requirement is\nthen <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math></span>. The freedom\nto select <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>T</mi></math></span> matters: this is not an\nestimate on a sample prescribed in advance, such as all prime\npositions.</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em><em>Four integral tail differences.</em> For <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and positive integers <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></math></span>, the conjunction </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em>\nis equivalent to <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span> alone. The affine\ntransport identity for <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">↦</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>H</mi></math></span>\npreserves integrality, so the three additional conditions add no\nrestriction. Neither <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi></math></span> nor <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi></math></span> need be prime.</em></p></li>\n</ol>\n<p><em>These three equivalences explain why these particular\nreformulations retain the original arithmetic question. They do not rule\nout useful weaker intermediate lemmas. The full-block and fixed-margin\nconditions in §<a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.html#sec:survivors\">3</a>\nask for additional quantitative information that the three arguments\nabove do not supply.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface#prop:b4","Failure of a specified two-adic\ncongruence construction","<p><em> A certificate requires the residue to lie\nfarther than <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> from either\nendpoint modulo <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></msup></math></span>. In the\nspecific construction below, the residue equals <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></span> modulo <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></msup></math></span>, but the defining congruence is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.444em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>mod</mi><mspace width=\"0.333em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. Hence <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></span>. At <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi></math></span>, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></math></span>, the error bound is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></span>, so the residue does not\nsatisfy the certificate inequalities. This calculation defeats this\nconstruction at every depth. It does not prove a corresponding statement\nfor every use of the Chinese Remainder Theorem or every prescribed\ntotient pattern.</em></p>"]],"source":"erdos249-totient-reasoning-surface.json?v=e6abdbcd8877"}
